+			    tail of chunk 1 is still in the ring makes the guest read
+			    back ITS OWN INJECTED BYTES as disk data.  The witness is
+			    at regress/artifacts/wdcaddtoinbufbound/rung3_20260830/.
+
+			    AND IT WAS SILENT.  The one diagnostic that could have
+			    announced a stray write requires !atapi_cmd_in_progress,
+			    and that flag is 1 for the whole of DATA-IN -- so the
+			    single guard that might have caught this was disabled
+			    exactly when it was needed.
+
+			    THE TEST IS THE PHASE, NOT THE FLAG, AND THE DIFFERENCE
+			    IS NOT COSMETIC.  #477 measured that guarding these
+			    pushes could CREATE a use-after-free: a suppressed push
